WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.462 --> 00:00:01.920
RYAN MATSUMOTO:
Today we're talking

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.990
about cloud adoption,
data analytics

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.760
training, and GraphQL.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.760
I'm Ryan, and welcome to "This
Week in Cloud," where we serve

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.290
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:13.540
Google Cloud commissioned
Coalition Greenwich

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.810
to survey 102 institutional
capital markets professionals

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:19.210
to understand the dynamics
behind their rapid adoption

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.640
of cloud technology and
found that the demand

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.070
for easier accessibility
was a huge factor.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:26.710
Check out the blog for more
insights and our top five

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.370
takeaways.

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:31.520
BigQuery is a fully managed
enterprise data warehouse

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:32.960
that helps you
manage and analyze

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.330
your data with built-in
features like machine

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:38.570
learning, geospatial analysis,
and intelligent caching

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:40.280
for business intelligence.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.960
To help you make the
most of BigQuery,

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.240
we're offering no-cost,
on-demand training

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:47.120
opportunities, including how
to use BigQuery with Looker

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.560
and machine learning.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.820
Check out the blog for
more details and links.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.710
Picking the right
API style completely

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:55.990
depends on your use
case, and GraphQL

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:58.210
is a query language
for APIs and a runtime

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:01.030
for fulfilling those queries
with your existing data.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:02.950
Developers are
increasingly adopting it

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.900
for its flexibility
and ease of use.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.780
And we're excited to announce
that Apigee API management

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:11.200
platform natively supports
GraphQL APIs, allowing

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.030
developers to
productize and manage

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:14.800
their lifecycle in Apigee.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.277
Check out the blog
for more information.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:19.360
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.890
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.380
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.130
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:27.630
We'll see you in the cloud.

